    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2S93TVbsGC5xPCxnTXaq4qi)_\n\n## What\n- New module `sp-batch-report` (doc `docs/tangles/funct/sp-batch-report.org`, tests `tests/sp-batch-report-test.el`):\n  - `sp-batch-report-file-link`, `-file-links`, `-note-link` make Org links (`[[file:/abs/path][name]]`).\n  - `sp-batch-report-mode`: a read-only Org buffer. `RET` visits the link, `n`/`p` move between links, `g` runs the command again, `q` closes.\n  - `sp-batch-report-show` fills the buffer (optional refresh function and derived mode).\n- Every file in these reports is now a link and the buffer is that mode:\n  - `sp-litnotes-titles-dryrun` and the first half of `-convert`\n  - `sp-litnotes-refs-dryrun` and the first half of `-convert`\n  - `sp-litnotes-meta-fill-all-dryrun` and `-convert`\n  - `sp-notes-filing-dryrun` (keeps `C-c C-c`)\n  - the property and keyword conversion previews (`sp-vulpea-convert-*`)\n\n## How far `vulpea-doctor` was reused\n- It builds one string (title, sections, aligned lines, an Issues list) and shows it in a `special-mode` buffer. It has no links, no keys, no refresh and no per-item actions, and it is a function, not a library.\n- So only its look was kept (title, sections, read-only buffer, `q`). Its `special-mode` buffer could not hold followable links, so the shared buffer is a read-only Org buffer.\n- Left as they were, because they already have `RET` to visit a line: author notes report, footnote lint, tag lint, Org normalise, BibTeX lint, the litnote status table. `sp-author-notes-works-dryrun` is a one-line message.\n\n## Tests\n- 8 new tests for the module, plus new or updated tests for titles, refs, meta, notes filing and the keyword preview. All pass in Emacs 29 with stubs, except `sp-litnotes-titles-bib-authors-surname`, which also fails on `main` (it calls `sp-author-notes-latex-to-unicode` without loading `sp-author-notes`).\n- Docs tangle to the committed `.el` files (whitespace aside).\n- Not run on the real vault or in Emacs 31.\n\nNo CHANGELOG edits, per the nightly-tidy rule.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAL5ZmmWoUzkvAu37X)_",
